### SafePaws: accounts, login and announcement changes
#
# Ready-made requests for the API in docs/api.md. Start the database and the backend first
# (see backend/README.md). The accounts are the demo accounts seeded by V6__users_and_owners.sql
# (listed in the root README); they are local demo data only.
#
# Format: IntelliJ IDEA HTTP Client. Run the requests from top to bottom.
# - IntelliJ: "Log in as Ana" saves the token automatically in {{token}} (the `> {% ... %}` script),
#   and "Log in as Mihai" saves {{mihaiToken}}.
# - VS Code REST Client: the automatic token capture only works in IntelliJ. Run the login request,
#   copy the "token" from the response and add these lines at the top of the file:
#     @token = <paste Ana's token here>
#     @mihaiToken = <paste Mihai's token here>
#
# Tokens are valid for 24 hours. Edit and resolve change the data; to get the demo data back,
# run `docker compose down -v`, then `docker compose up -d` and start the backend again.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@demoPassword = SafePaws1!
# Announcement 1 is Mitzi, owned by ana@safepaws.dev (V6)
@announcementId = 1

### Register a new account (public). Returns 201 with the user; a second run returns 409.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "new.user@example.com",
  "password": "{{demoPassword}}",
  "displayName": "New User"
}

### Log in as Ana (public). Returns the token, its expiry and the user.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ana@safepaws.dev",
  "password": "{{demoPassword}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.token);
%}

### Who am I? Needs the token; without it (or with an expired one) returns 401.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create an announcement (needs a token). Returns 201 and a Location header.
POST {{baseUrl}}/announcements
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "type": "LOST",
  "species": "DOG",
  "petName": "Bruno",
  "breed": "Mixed breed",
  "color": "Brown",
  "distinctiveMarks": "Blue collar, white spot on the chest",
  "eventDate": "2026-11-15T09:30:00",
  "latitude": 46.7700,
  "longitude": 23.5900,
  "area": "Centru, Cluj-Napoca",
  "contactName": "Ana Pop",
  "contactPhone": "0711111111"
}

### Edit announcement 1 as Ana, its owner (needs a token). PUT replaces every field:
### a field left out is cleared. Status, photos and owner do not change.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/announcements/{{announcementId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "type": "LOST",
  "species": "CAT",
  "petName": "Mitzi",
  "breed": "European",
  "color": "Grey with white paws",
  "distinctiveMarks": "Young kitten with blue eyes, white chest and paws, very playful. Wears a red collar.",
  "eventDate": "2026-11-10T18:00:00",
  "latitude": 46.7550,
  "longitude": 23.5560,
  "area": "Mănăștur, Cluj-Napoca",
  "contactName": "Ana Pop",
  "contactPhone": "0700000001"
}

### Resolve announcement 1 as Ana (needs a token). Send "ACTIVE" to show it again.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/announcements/{{announcementId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "status": "RESOLVED"
}

### Log in as Mihai (public), to try changing an announcement he does not own.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mihai@safepaws.dev",
  "password": "{{demoPassword}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("mihaiToken", response.body.token);
%}

### Mihai tries to edit Ana's announcement 1.
### Returns 403 Forbidden "Only the owner can modify this announcement"; nothing is saved.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/announcements/{{announcementId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{mihaiToken}}

{
  "type": "LOST",
  "species": "CAT",
  "petName": "Mitzi",
  "breed": "European",
  "color": "Grey with white paws",
  "distinctiveMarks": "Young kitten with blue eyes, white chest and paws, very playful. Wears a red collar.",
  "eventDate": "2026-11-10T18:00:00",
  "latitude": 46.7550,
  "longitude": 23.5560,
  "area": "Mănăștur, Cluj-Napoca",
  "contactName": "Ana Pop",
  "contactPhone": "0700000001"
}
